What:           /sys/kernel/gpu/gpu_memory
Date:           September 2026
KernelVersion:  4.19 (Alioth downstream)
Contact:        PocoF3Releases kernel maintainers
Description:
                Read-only compatibility link to
                /sys/class/kgsl/kgsl/page_alloc. Decimal bytes of tracked
                non-secure KGSL paged allocations, read atomically from
                kgsl_driver.stats.page_alloc. No GPU wake or hardware
                register access is performed by this read.

                This is not a dedicated VRAM total or a resident-memory
                measurement. It excludes separately accounted imported
                mappings, secure and coherent allocations. Reclaimable
                allocation backing need not all be resident. Do not add
                mapped or vmalloc to this number: accounting can overlap.
                Per-process/pagetable statistics and tuning controls are
                not exposed by this interface. Android SELinux policy must
                grant read access to the link and its exact target.

                Applications must implement a reader for this path or the
                original page_alloc path; creating a node alone cannot
                guarantee recognition by DevCheck or another application.
